: {"u": 861, "v": 480, "window": [14821, 53221]}, "result_digest": "4335266cba232550", "result_summary": "{\"connected\": false, \"n_events_u_to_v\": 0, \"n_events_v_to_u\": 0, \"u\": 861, \"v\": 480, \"window\": [14821, 53221]}", "latency_ms": 0, "tokens_before": 41058, "tokens_after": 41058, "ok": true, "error": ""}], "final_claim": {"task_id": "t_fd7e502f", "decision": "insufficient", "mechanism": "cascade", "entities": [318, 480], "window": [14821, 53221], "confidence": 0.7, "evidence": [{"trace_id": "step_01", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_05", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_09", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_10", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_11", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_12", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_13", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_14", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_15", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_16", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_02", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_03", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_04", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_07", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_06", "role": "confounder_control"}], "narrative": "I cannot confirm a time-respecting cascade from 318 to 480 in [14821,53221]. There is no direct 318\u2192480 event (step_01), and 318's out-neighbors (step_05) do not match 480's in-neighbors (step_07). Explicit checks for several primary intermediaries (250,259,409,436,603,652,735,861) show no events to 480 in the window (steps_09\u201316). However, the static k-hop subgraphs show connectivity when time is ignored (steps_02\u201303) and both nodes are active in the interval (step_04); these are potential confounders. The available aggregated queries do not provide ordered timestamps of individual events needed to verify a chain with successive gaps \u2264600, and the checks done do not exhaust all possible multi-hop temporal sequences, so the temporal evidence is insufficient to decide."}, "raw_final_response": "{\n  \"task_id\": \"t_fd7e502f\",\n  \"decision\": \"insufficient\",\n  \"mechanism\": \"cascade\",\n  \"entities\": [318, 480],\n  \"window\": [14821, 53221],\n  \"confidence\": 0.70,\n  \"evidence\": [\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_01\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_05\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_09\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_10\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_11\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_12\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_13\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_14\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_15\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_16\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_02\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_03\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_04\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_07\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_06\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"}\n  ],\n  \"narrative\": \"I cannot confirm a time-respecting cascade from 318 to 480 in [14821,53221]. There is no direct 318\u2192480 event (step_01), and 318's out-neighbors (step_05) do not match 480's in-neighbors (step_07). Explicit checks for several primary intermediaries (250,259,409,436,603,652,735,861) show no events to 480 in the window (steps_09\u201316). However, the static k-hop subgraphs show connectivity when time is ignored (steps_02\u201303) and both nodes are active in the interval (step_04); these are potential confounders. The available aggregated queries do not provide ordered timestamps of individual events needed to verify a chain with successive gaps \u2264600, and the checks done do not exhaust all possible multi-hop temporal sequences, so the temporal evidence is insufficient to decide.\"\n}", "total_input_tokens": 48314, "total_output_tokens": 6881, "total_tokens": 55195, "total_latency_ms": 92361, "llm_calls": 10, "schema_repairs": 0, "status": "success", "error": ""}